==Trivia==
*Inumusha means "dog warrior" in Japanese.
**Inumusha's name may also be a reference to the manga ''[[wikipedia:Inuyasha|Inuyasha]]'', which has a main character that is half dog and half human, who also uses a greatsword as a weapon.
*The title of the play in his Japanese description, "The Battle of Ganryu Island", refers to a legendary battle taking place at [[wikipedia:Ganryū-jima|Ganryu Island]], where the famed swordsman Miyamoto Musashi fought and dueled his rival, [[wikipedia:Sasaki Kojirō|Sasaki Kojirō]], and won with a wooden sword crafted from an oar.
*The "cursed castle" in his description refers to the [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]] in [[Multiversal Studios]], [[Multiplanar Studios]] and [[Bowl of Bliss]].
*Inumusha appears in the 37th sub-chapters of both [[Stories of Legend]] ([[Walk of Fame]]) and [[Zero Legends]] ([[Noodle Nirvana]]).
*Inumusha being the fourth [[:Category:Mythic Bosses|Mythic Boss]] of Stories of Legend, having 40,000 attack power, taking 4 seconds to revive and dropping a minimum of 4,000¢ is likely a reference to how, in Japanese, one of the two pronunciations for the number 4 sounds exactly like the Japanese word for death.
*He is the only [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] [[:Category:Enemy Cats|Enemy Cat]].
*He has the highest knockback count of all Zombies.

